":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7637","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7637","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7637.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7637.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-16T10:56:44Z"},"body":"For #5996 (task 12996). Decision doc only — no code implementation, per the issue's scope.\n\nAdds `doc/2026-11-08T10-26-00Z_design_id5996_hot_swap_decision/` — the hot-swap alternatives decision record for #5964 (dynamic user functions):\n\n- Compares all three mechanisms (Wasm component dynamic instantiation; restart with warm compile cache; interpreted behavior layer) on the issue's five axes — swap latency at tick boundary, isolation, metering compatibility, determinism for replay, implementation cost — against the current host as verified fresh at `0865aad9a9` (`world_compile.rs` compile + BLAKE3 identity scheme, `sandbox.rs` Wasmtime fuel metering, `install_wasm` atomic install with keep-previous fallback, `plaza_snapshot`/`plaza_restore` state handoff).\n- **Decision: v1 is mechanism 2, realized as instance-per-function restart** — per-function Wasm modules swapped by fresh instantiation at tick boundaries, warm cache keyed by the existing provenance digests; failed compiles/instantiations leave the published version running.\n- Names the rejected alternatives with reasons (components: immature dynamic linking + no host runtime today; interpreted layer: abandons the server-compiled-Roc requirement and adds a second metering stack) and the triggers that would reopen the decision (component maturity, measured swap latency, native-tier functions, non-programmer authoring, cache-hit collapse).\n- Consistent with the sibling #5967 mapping design (tick-boundary rebinds, state handover only by explicit rule).\n\n🤖 Queue worker lane code-e (task 12996)\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796725690&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7637&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7637&signature=cb30f2e345cff0b0257f5eb9836b40f68cd5deb14ea68adca511764c86677912\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7637?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7637/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7637/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/10746","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/10746/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/10746/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/10746/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/10746","id":6421583532,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABPiC9vg","number":10746,"title":"docs(id): dynamic user functions design (#5964)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:complete","name":"audit:complete","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-11-16T12:50:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T01:14:37Z","closed_at":"2026-11-16T12:53:43Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/10746","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/10746","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/10746.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/10746.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-16T12:53:43Z"},"body":"Design doc for #5964 (task 17477, follow-on from triage task 15250), written after all research gates landed and verified fresh:\n\n- #5995 CLOSED — Roc evidence (PR #8478): tracked compiler has no library/DLL output; legacy `libapp.so` is startup linking only. The doc carries no DLL premise.\n- #5966 CLOSED — per-function gas/timeout research.\n- #5996 decision LANDED — PR #7637 merged 2026-11-16: v1 = instance-per-function restart.\n\nThe doc covers the issue's five Done-criteria areas: (1) interface contract — name/version/interface-hash identity, discovery via the #5967 mapping, mismatch refuses activation and keeps the previously published version (the stated default); (2) server compile pipeline — source-only (C3), tracked compiler `wasm32`, provenance triple, persistent content-addressed warm cache; (3) placement/binding — publish-then-swap, tick-boundary activation, in-flight calls finish on the old instance, host-owned snapshot state handoff; (4) failure fallbacks and isolation — per-function fuel budget inside the world per-tick budget, poisoned-instance discard, uniform keep-published fallback; (5) the trust argument end-to-end — server-compiled provenance, only world-author-passed platform capabilities are non-pure. It states what v1 defers (component-model dynamic instantiation, native per-function processes) and distinguishes the authoring hot-swap loop (#558/#5541). Design only; no implementation.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797425427&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=10746&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F10746&signature=e4fb0d8db843d01f471fcc1d33fd14c4da59816a2645b2cd838cf4853ac235a4\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/10746?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added a design document outlining dynamic per-user functions, including versioning, validation, resource limits, state transfer, and failure handling.\n  * The design describes a proposed approach; no implementation changes were made.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/10746/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/10746/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7600","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7600/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7600/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7600/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7600","id":6269422320,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNovvcQ","number":7600,"title":"doc(id): conversation archaeology — worlds tie-in record and C1–C4 rulings (#5990)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:complete","name":"audit:complete","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-11-08T09:10:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T06:16:45Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T19:53:19Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7600","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7600","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7600.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7600.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T19:53:19Z"},"body":"Lands the conversation-archaeology tie-in for the worlds program as a `doc/` record, which is the deliverable of #5990 that until now existed only as issue comments on #5955.\n\n## What this adds\n\n- `doc/2026-11-08T09-10-00Z_research_worlds_conversation_archaeology/…md` — the tie-in record:\n  - **F1/F2** (founding dictation, OpenCode session `ses_ef03b7d73ffewFUtEk0FCMTiz5`, 2026-10-06 → 10-07) with Drew's 2026-10-07 quote preserved verbatim, plus the Second Life / There.com / ActiveWorlds / Habbo / Gaia / Goblins / E-lang / Cap'n Proto RPC / Veilid / Anoma inspiration set.\n  - **C1–C4 rulings** (Drew, 2026-11-04 23:57 CST) reproduced in full, including the C2 correction (the shipped isolated seccomp default does not move) and the C3/C4 iteration doctrine.\n  - A classification table against the #5955 design children: *consistent* / *superseded by the 2026-11-04 brief* / *in tension — needs Drew*.\n  - The child pointer-comment table, spot-checked: all nine children named by the ruling comment carry theirs.\n- `doc/README.md` — index entry for the new record.\n\n## What this deliberately does not do\n\n- **No new archaeology.** Every recovered thread is quoted or paraphrased from the cited comments, with their dates and session references preserved.\n- **Nothing flagged in tension is resolved.** The C1 uploads regime stays open and owned by #5984; the record says so explicitly.\n- **F3–F12 bodies are not reconstructed.** They live only in `workspace/scratch/worlds-capabilities-brief-2026-11-04/conversation-tie-ins.md`, which is outside the repository and not present on the machine this was written from. The record names this as a known gap with a follow-up path (append when the file is recovered) rather than inventing findings.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `doc/README.md` link target exists at the recorded path.\n- Child pointer comments verified present via `gh api` on 2026-11-08 for #5984, #5977, #5958, #5957, #5962, #5964, #5996, #5966, #6001.\n\nCloses #5990 once merged (the doc is linked from #5955 and #5990 in follow-up comments).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796721056&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7600&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7600&signature=5e851f1d33a986cdec5c699e931e074df26159167a5bd3f629a04578a2209113\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7600?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled --